    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d93">

                <pb facs="0137" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1945v07/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.458/7–545: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hurley</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-05">July 5, 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1040. Please communicate to FonOff following message from me to Dr. T. V. Soong:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Today<anchor n="59" xml:id="d93-f1"/> it is eight full years since your
                            country made its momentous decision to resist Japanese aggression. On
                            this occasion it is a privilege for me to join with other Americans in
                            doing honor to the unconquerable spirit that has inspired the Chinese
                            people to carry on so bravely despite long trials and grievous
                            sacrifices.</p>
                        <p>The rapid progress of the present Allied drives against the Japanese and
                            the solid achievements of the San Francisco Conference give ground for
                            high hopes that, through our continuing determined and concerted
                            efforts, we may not only accomplish the relatively early defeat of the
                            last of the Axis aggressors, but also provide effective assurance that
                            such aggressors can not rise again to scourge mankind.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
